---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

// An Orthodox Table — the front of the parish recipe collection.
// Two shelves, side by side on one row: the fasting book and everything
// else. Deliberately only two choices, because a cook arriving here
// already knows which kind of day it is.
---

<Layout
  title="An Orthodox Table | St. John of Kronstadt Orthodox Mission"
  description="Recipes and a guide to eating Orthodox — fasting dishes and everyday cooking shared by our parish."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-12 md:px-6">
    <p class="font-display text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-tan-dark">
      St. John of Kronstadt Orthodox Mission
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-4xl text-text-primary md:text-5xl">An Orthodox Table</h1>
    <div class="mt-5 h-px w-24 bg-liturgical-current"></div>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl font-display text-lg text-text-primary/85 md:text-xl">
      Recipes and a guide to eating Orthodox.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-text-primary/85 leading-relaxed">
      The Church keeps roughly half the year as fast, and a fast is not a
      hardship to be endured in silence — it has its own cooking, handed
      between households for centuries. These are our parish's, shared by
      the people who make them.
    </p>

    <!-- Two entry points on one row, as asked. They fall to one column on
         a phone rather than squeezing to half-width each. -->
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <a
        href="/table/fasting/"
        class="group block border border-border-soft bg-cream-card p-7 no-underline shadow-sm transition-colors hover:border-brand-blue-dark"
      >
        <span class="font-display text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-tan-dark">Book One</span>
        <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl text-text-primary group-hover:text-brand-blue-dark">
          Fasting Recipes
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-4 h-px w-16 bg-liturgical-current"></div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-text-primary/85 leading-relaxed">
          No meat, dairy or eggs. What we cook on Wednesdays and Fridays,
          through Great Lent, and the other fasts of the year.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 font-display text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-blue-dark">
          Open the fasting book →
        </p>
      </a>

      <a
        href="/table/everyday/"
        class="group block border border-border-soft bg-cream-card p-7 no-underline shadow-sm transition-colors hover:border-brand-blue-dark"
      >
        <span class="font-display text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-tan-dark">Book Two</span>
        <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl text-text-primary group-hover:text-brand-blue-dark">
          Everyday Recipes
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-4 h-px w-16 bg-liturgical-current"></div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-text-primary/85 leading-relaxed">
          Feast days, Pascha, coffee hour, and anything else our people
          want to pass along.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 font-display text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-blue-dark">
          Open the everyday book →
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-border-soft pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-text-primary">Share one of yours</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-text-primary/85 leading-relaxed">
        Catechumens and members can add recipes to either book. Fill in the
        form and it comes to the parish office; once it's been looked over
        it goes up with your name on it.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5">
        <a href="/table/share/" class="btn btn-primary">Share a recipe</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-border-soft pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-text-primary">What the fast asks</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-text-primary/85 leading-relaxed">
        The fasting rule for any given day is on the
        <a href="/calendar/" class="font-semibold text-brand-blue-dark">parish calendar</a> —
        it says plainly whether the day is a fast, whether fish, wine or oil
        are allowed, and which season it belongs to. When in doubt, ask Fr.
        Antonios rather than a website.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
